            "count": 0,
            "text": "Created attachment 3760\nUse VEH to print a traceback when crashing on Windows\n\nCurrently, when a package crashes on Win-Builder during tests or examples, the output just stops. It takes effort to determine that there was, in fact, a crash (and not timeout / storage becoming full / hardware issues / gremlins), and there's not always enough information to determine where the crash occurred. Sometimes we're lucky and the crash [is easily reproducible](https://stat.ethz.ch/pipermail/r-package-devel/2026q2/012376.html). [Other times](https://stat.ethz.ch/pipermail/r-package-devel/2023q4/010170.html) the crash [remains elusive](https://stat.ethz.ch/pipermail/r-package-devel/2026q3/012434.html) and we're stumped until we can obtain more information (with luck, the same crash shows up with sanitizers on Linux).\n\nConversely, on most Unix-like systems (with working `sigaction()` and `sigaltstack()`), the signal handler makes the crash evident and (if the heap is sufficiently intact) provides an R-level traceback. On Windows, R could use [vectored exception handling](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/debug/vectored-exception-handling) to catch a fatal exception in a similar manner. \n\nThe attached patch takes the common, R-specific parts of `sigactionSegv` and `win32_segv` ([unused](https://stat.ethz.ch/pipermail/r-devel/2024-June/083524.html)) and makes R call them from the respective system-specific handlers. Currently it's wired up to minimise changes in `src/main/main.c` and to leave Windows-specific code under `src/gnuwin32`, although the result feels awkward. Perhaps it's better to make `fatal_traceback()` declared in `Defn.h`, `attribute_hidden`, to be called from handlers registered in `src/main/main.c` or `src/gnuwin32/system.c`?\n\n```\n$ ../../bin/x64/Rscript.exe -e '.Fortran(stats:::C_lowesw, numeric(), 100L, numeric(), integer())'\n\n *** caught access violation at address 0x00007ffb33252192 ***\naccessing address 0xffffffffffffffff, action: read\n\nTraceback:\n 1: .Fortran(stats:::C_lowesw, numeric(), 100L, numeric(), integer())\nAn irrecoverable exception occurred. R is aborting now ...\n```",
